    "sourceReview": [
      "Each birth stores hull support position, actual horizontal direction, time, strength, stable seed and segment. Later geometry uses only those immutable values and age.",
      "Age independently spreads, drifts and fades an open crest; only rendered Y follows current tide. New journeys preserve existing events and never connect their geometry.",
      "finish ends emission without recording a live hull contact or trip-peak docking flourish. Normal residual lifetime is bounded by 1800ms. clear removes all transients.",
      "Horizontal displacement drives emission. Pure yaw, idle bobbing, tide and draft motion do not create travel waves.",
      "Same borrowed coast mask, depth test, disabled depth writes, one decorative nonpickable mesh excluded from camera bounds."
    ],
